[% set v = c.values_ref %]
[% set h = c.helper %]
{{- /*
===============================================================================
ServiceAccount of the "[[ c.name ]]" component
===============================================================================
File generated by forge.

Gives [[ c.name ]] an identity of its own with the Kubernetes API. Without it,
the pods run under the "default" account of the namespace, whose rights are
shared by everything deployed there: it then becomes impossible to grant a
permission to this component alone.

Two points to watch, both handled by the naming helper:
  * the workload must set "serviceAccountName" via
    {{ include "[[ h ]].serviceAccountName" . }} — that is what the workload
    template does; without that line, the account would be created without ever
    being used;
  * when serviceAccount.create is false, the chart creates nothing and the
    workload references serviceAccount.name — which must then designate an
    existing account, on pain of pods stuck at startup. Left empty, the helper
    falls back on "default", which always exists.

No value is hardcoded here. Everything comes from the
"[[ c.name ]].serviceAccount" key of values.yaml, overridable per environment.
===============================================================================
*/}}
{{- if and [[ v ]].enabled [[ v ]].serviceAccount.create }}
apiVersion: v1
kind: ServiceAccount
metadata:
  name: {{ include "[[ h ]].serviceAccountName" . }}
  labels:
    {{- include "[[ h ]].labels" . | nindent 4 }}
  {{- /*
    The annotations carry the federated identity of the cloud provider
    (eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn, iam.gke.io/gcp-service-account, …). The block
    disappears entirely when the table is empty: "annotations:" with no element
    would amount to null and would be refused.
  */}}
  {{- with [[ v ]].serviceAccount.annotations }}
  annotations:
    {{- toYaml . | nindent 4 }}
  {{- end }}
{{- /*
  Mounts, or does not mount, the API token in the pods that use this account.
  False as long as [[ c.name ]] does not call the Kubernetes API: that is one
  secret fewer exposed in the container.
*/}}
automountServiceAccountToken: {{ [[ v ]].serviceAccount.automountServiceAccountToken }}
{{- end }}
